    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4315" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attălēa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attălīa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτταλεία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>name of a Greek city.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>In the region of Mysia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30,
				32, § 121</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>On the coast of Pamphylia</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act.
				14, 25</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>In Galatia;</i> v. Attalenses.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
